# A100 deployment parameters (A100 80 GB, compute capability 8.0): configs/h100.env's parameters — the same variables, probes, refusals and
# JIT-cache keying (MODEL_OPT_STACK_KEY is derived from the interpreter on PATH and the visible card on either: torch2.13.0-cu130-sm80 here) —
# with this card's one value, the target-GPU word, set first. usage: `run.sh design|check|warm --config a100 --mode <mode> ...`, or
# `source configs/a100.env` before `RFDIFFUSION3_OPT=exact rfd3 design ...` in the patched interpreter. Either A100 (80 GB or 40 GB) runs every
# mode and lever: the levers read the card from the device, not from this word — the fused transition (RFD3_FZT) serves the shared core's 8.0
# cells at the row counts of its 8.0 range (patched layers/layer_utils.py FZT_ROWS_BY_CC: `128x256` from 16384 rows, the other cells from
# 4096, all up to 1048544; outside it the stock statements run by name, `cells_stock['rows<MIN:<cell>']`, and the `APPLIED … layer_utils`
# line says `rows_cc=8.0 rows_served=…`), so `exact` == this card's own `off` bit for bit under `--det 1` at every size; a cell without an
# 8.0 row in the core's table would fall back to the stock transition by name (`[rfdiffusion3-opt] FALLBACK lever=RFD3_FZT …`, a partial
# activation: CHANGES.md); the gather kernel and the compiled denoiser take their 8.0 rows / sm_80 code from the running card. Memory is the
# one difference between the two A100s and it is probed, not configured: the atom-attention pre-flight reads the device's free memory, so
# the 40 GB card holds a smaller diffusion_batch_size at a given length and refuses (or CUDA reports out of memory) by name beyond it.
export MODEL_OPT_TARGET_GPU=${MODEL_OPT_TARGET_GPU:-A100}                                                            # the GPU this configuration targets (compute capability 8.0); check reports what it sees
. "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/h100.env"                                                                            # keep this line last: configs/h100.env's refusals (its return codes) are this file's
